      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Qubits and Superposition\n   - Definition of Qubits\n   - Superposition principle\n   - Mathematical representation of superposition\n   - Measurement and collapse of superposition\n   - Applications of superposition in quantum computing\n   - Superposition and parallelism\n\n2. Quantum Entanglement\n   - Introduction to entanglement\n   - Bell's theorem and its implications\n   - Entanglement and non-locality\n   - Entanglement in quantum communication\n   - Entanglement-based protocols (e.g., teleportation)\n\n3. Quantum Gates and Circuits\n   - Introduction to quantum gates\n   - Single qubit gates (X, Y, Z, H, S, T)\n   - Multi-qubit gates (CNOT, SWAP)\n   - Quantum circuits and their role in computation\n   - Building and analyzing quantum circuits\n   - Quantum error correction and fault tolerance\n\n4. Basic Algorithms\n   - Introduction to quantum algorithms\n   - Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm\n   - Grover's algorithm\n   - Shor's algorithm\n   - Quantum Fourier Transform\n   - Quantum algorithms for optimization and search\n\n5. Hardware Implementations\n   - Overview of quantum hardware",
      "source": "target",
